A computer-implemented method for controlling access to a restricted resource of a resource provider in a network-connected computer system, wherein a blockchain data structure accessible via the network stores digitally signed records validated by network-connected miner software components, the method comprising:

- identifying an access-control role definition governing access to the resource, the role including a specification of access permissions;
- defining a cryptocurrency that indicates authorization to access the resource, the cryptocurrency comprising tradable units of value associated with records in the blockchain, wherein transfers of the cryptocurrency between records in the blockchain are validated by the miners;
- receiving, from an authenticated resource consumer, a request for authorization to access the resource; and
- submitting a blockchain transaction to the miner components to transfer a quantity of the cryptocurrency to a consumer record in the blockchain, the transaction including an identification of the role, such that the consumer record indicates that the consumer is authorized to access the resource in accordance with the role definition.

